From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] context: use EspLocation when UDisks finds no ESP

fwupd.conf(5) describes EspLocation as the ESP path to use when UDisks
cannot identify it, but the ESP list is only ever built from UDisks, so on
a system without UDisks (it needs polkit) EspLocation is never consulted
and the UEFI capsule plugin reports "UEFI ESP partition not detected", which
makes every capsule-on-disk device non-updatable.

When no ESP was found, fall back to a volume at EspLocation if it is a
mounted ESP (has an EFI directory), as the FWUPD_UEFI_ESP_PATH test path
already does.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/libfwupdplugin/fu-context.c	2026-10-25 22:07:47.573655542 -0400
+++ b/libfwupdplugin/fu-context.c	2026-10-25 22:07:57.866803587 -0400
@@ -1705,6 +1705,9 @@
 	return priv->esp_location;
 }
 
+static gboolean
+fu_context_is_esp(FuVolume *esp);
+
 /**
  * fu_context_get_esp_volumes:
  * @self: a #FuContext
@@ -1779,6 +1782,18 @@
 	if (priv->esp_volumes->len == 0) {
 		g_autoptr(GPtrArray) devices = NULL;
 
+		/* no UDisks to identify the ESP: trust the configured EspLocation
+		 * when it is a mounted ESP, as fwupd.conf(5) describes it */
+		if (priv->esp_location != NULL) {
+			g_autoptr(FuVolume) vol = fu_volume_new_from_mount_path(priv->esp_location);
+			fu_volume_set_partition_kind(vol, FU_VOLUME_KIND_ESP);
+			if (fu_context_is_esp(vol)) {
+				fu_context_add_esp_volume(self, vol);
+				return g_ptr_array_ref(priv->esp_volumes);
+			}
+			g_debug("EspLocation %s is not an ESP", priv->esp_location);
+		}
+
 		/* check if udisks2 is working */
 		devices = fu_common_get_block_devices(error);
 		if (devices == NULL)
